course: dictionary
lesson: 2781
title: A word from the kitchen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dishcloth is a cloth you use to wash or wipe dishes, cups and pans. You will find one in almost every kitchen, so it is a useful word to know.
explain: Context helps you here. In old books you might read «a dish-clout». The sentence is about a kitchen, and a clout is an old word for a cloth, so it means a dishcloth. Look at the words around an unknown word and ask what would fit there.
explain: A damp dishcloth can grow germs, so wash it and let it dry often. This is why a dishcloth is more than a dirty rag: it keeps the kitchen clean.
fact: A dishcloth is a cloth used for washing or wiping dishes, cups and pans.
fact: «Dishcloth» is made from two smaller words: dish and cloth.
fact: In the UK, a cloth for drying dishes is sometimes also called a dishcloth, but most people call it a tea towel.
fact: Damp cloths can grow germs, so wash your dishcloth and let it dry often.
fact: In old books you might find «a dish-clout», which is an older word for a dishcloth.
exercise: In an old book you read «a dish-clout». What does it mean? | *A dishcloth | A broom for sweeping the floor | A kind of hat
exercise: Why should you wash and dry a dishcloth often? | Dishcloths shrink when they are dry | *Damp cloths can grow germs | Wet cloths keep cups warm | Dishcloths are only for the bathroom
exercise: In the UK, what do most people call a cloth used for drying dishes? | Dishcloth | Mop | Sponge | *Tea towel
test: Which of these is used for washing or wiping dishes, cups and pans? | Towel for your bath | *Dishcloth | Oven glove | Duster for the shelves
test: Lily says a dishcloth is a sort of plant. What is it really? | *A cloth for washing or wiping dishes | A kind of plate | A cup with a handle | A plant with wide leaves
exam: Which sentence uses dishcloth correctly? | *Dad rinsed the dishcloth and hung it out to dry. | The dishcloth was a loud red bus. | He wore the dishcloth to school on Monday. | The dog barked at the dishcloth and ran away.
